From a46f594db94192698e0a9378bd8828d347924858 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:36:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: maintain a pinned incremental reconciliation window

Advance admission-time cursors and per-ID occurrence counts instead of rebuilding an all-window seen hash set on every reconciliation. Maintain a persistent numeric-ID candidate tree and pin it under the index writer lock; enumerate candidates and resolve transaction refs from a pinned published mempool view outside both index and mempool mutexes.

Apply the4096 cap after live membership and non-coinbase filtering, preserving the existing numeric minimum-ID set and roots. Keep the original scan API as a differential oracle. Rebuild for backwards query ranges/epoch changes and preserve the original reverse-scan semantics during out-of-order admission timestamps; pruning the inverted edges restores incremental operation.

Add deterministic mutation/epoch/prune/window-edge equivalence checks and a lagging-live-membership cap counterexample with root/bucket equality and short-ID collisions. Generic radix copies retain writer synchronization; stable-root pinning is protected by the index writer mutex. Source-only: diff checks pass, native build/tests and A-B remain pending.

Coordinator integration: fold reviewed actual-tree concurrent join/cap/root tests155f/fdd/7b, bounded waits and zero-callback cleanup. Existing source stable-root cloning prerequisite precedes this purpose. Indexed time-window occurrences and pinned published-mempool live membership retain original numeric4096LIVE cap, timing exclusions, collision behavior and fallback; no consensus change.

Coordinator validated lifetime repair: dedicated WindowEntryAdapter returns the numeric key by value instead of forwarding a reference to a temporary. No extra stored key or generic radix behavior change. Existing pinned-index oracle/live-cap tests pass and compiler dangling-reference warning is removed.

